      "writtenOn": "2016-06-30T22:49:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Disabling HOST_HIGH doesn\u0027t put the high side into hi-z; it actually connects the two CC pins together with 24.18k resistance.  This isn\u0027t enough to be considered \"open\" from the type-c spec, and is really here just to save power when DEVICE_ODL is asserted low.\n\nSo Glados should be treated the same as Samus in that it cannot truly go hi-z.",
      "revId": "6faf9c34e61f25aca62f864efb600e922057c2a4",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fd43127f_6d314192",
        "filename": "board/glados_pd/usb_pd_config.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 256,
      "author": {
        "id": 1146300
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-06-30T23:55:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Bummer. I\u0027ll see if I can simulate CC_OPEN/High-z instead.",
      "parentUuid": "fd43127f_f2e1b031",
      "revId": "6faf9c34e61f25aca62f864efb600e922057c2a4",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8082ab4f_4cb6f3eb",
        "filename": "board/glados_pd/usb_pd_config.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 256,
      "author": {
        "id": 1146300
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-07-01T12:53:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The requirement is to disconnect any resistors from CC1/CC2 (both Rd and Rp) so the remote side sees the link as disconnected. Is there any way to do this with those products ?",
      "parentUuid": "fd43127f_f2e1b031",
      "revId": "6faf9c34e61f25aca62f864efb600e922057c2a4",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fa1a38b3_3b766bf0",
        "filename": "board/glados_pd/usb_pd_config.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 256,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002022
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-07-12T03:33:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nope.  The best way to do it is to flip to the opposite state to force a disconnect:\n\n\"A port may choose not to support the ErrorRecovery state. If the ErrorRecovery state is not supported, the port shall be directed to the Disabled state if supported. If the Disabled state is not supported, the port shall be directed to either the Unattached.SNK or Unattached.SRC states.\"\n\nSo if you\u0027re in Attached.SRC and you want to force a disconnect, you would go into Unattached.SNK.\n\nIf you want to make sure *nothing* connects to you, the only option is to go into Unattached.SRC but never apply VBUS.",
      "parentUuid": "8082ab4f_4cb6f3eb",
      "revId": "6faf9c34e61f25aca62f864efb600e922057c2a4",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fa1a38b3_0dd37236",
        "filename": "board/glados_pd/usb_pd_config.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 256,
      "author": {
        "id": 1146300
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-07-12T14:32:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would be nice if that worked, but several of the adapters I tested simply won\u0027t reconnect unless they get a complete disconnect after a protocol error. Such error states are easy to trigger, for example by resetting the protocol engine (or rebooting the system) in a connected state. Disconnecting power doesn\u0027t help if power is applied from the other end.\nThe only alternative is to physically disconnect the adapters in such cases.",
      "parentUuid": "fa1a38b3_3b766bf0",
      "revId": "6faf9c34e61f25aca62f864efb600e922057c2a4",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fa1a38b3_c07629bd",
        "filename": "board/glados_pd/usb_pd_config.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 256,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002022
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-07-13T23:52:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Swapping to an Rp isn\u0027t sufficient?  Unfortunately, there\u0027s not much we can do on these gen-1 systems if that\u0027s the case.",
      "parentUuid": "fa1a38b3_0dd37236",
      "revId": "6faf9c34e61f25aca62f864efb600e922057c2a4",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
